# Scheduled jobs for directory.kiamclinic.com
#
# Install into the container's crontab, or point a host scheduler at the same
# commands. Times are the container's TZ — set TZ=Europe/London so 03:00 means
# 03:00 to a UK practitioner reading the resulting email.
#
# Both jobs are idempotent and safe to re-run: the sweep recomputes from
# evidence, and the reindex rewrites vectors from the current rows. A missed
# night is caught up by the next one, with one exception noted below.

TZ=Europe/London
SHELL=/bin/sh
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# 03:00 — expire stale checks, recompute badges and under-18 gating, send the
# 60/30/7/0-day reminders and any provisional-lapse notices.
#
# NOTE: reminders are keyed on an exact days-remaining bucket, so a night that
# does not run is a reminder nobody receives. If the job fails, re-run it the
# same day rather than waiting — see directory/services/verification.py.
0 3 * * * cd /app && python manage.py verification_sweep >> /var/log/kiam/verification_sweep.log 2>&1

# 03:30 — rebuild search vectors. Safety net behind the signals, and the only
# thing that picks up a synonym added to taxonomy.py (which changes the
# Speciality row, not the Practitioner, so nothing signals).
30 3 * * * cd /app && python manage.py rebuild_search_index >> /var/log/kiam/search_index.log 2>&1

# 04:00 — delete evidence whose retention period has elapsed.
#
# `Document.delete_after` is set by publication.request_removal() when a
# practitioner asks to be removed, and the dashboard tells them the documents are
# deleted automatically after a period. This is what makes that true. Runs AFTER
# the verification sweep and the reindex: a document disappearing mid-sweep would
# make the sweep's own reasoning about evidence wrong.
#
# The retention period itself is EVIDENCE_RETENTION_DAYS and is a solicitor
# question — see docs/verification-policy.md and the TODO(sign-off) in base.py.
0 4 * * * cd /app && python manage.py purge_expired_evidence >> /var/log/kiam/retention.log 2>&1
